  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GAP phase 2, Min for HR and Refugees (FIGAP) - GAP phase 2, Min for HR and Refugees (FIGAP) old strategy</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">J&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetshandlingsplan fas 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till Bosnien och Hercegovinas j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsmyndighet (Gender Equality Agency p&#xe5; statlig niv&#xe5; och tv&#xe5; myndigheter p&#xe5; entitetsniv&#xe5;). M&#xe5;let med insatsen &#xe4;r att genom standardiserad j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering uppn&#xe5; att allm&#xe4;nna beslut f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrar villkoren f&#xf6;r kvinnor, m&#xe4;n, flickor och pojkar i Bosnien p&#xe5; ett j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;llt sett och att en standardiserad j&#xe4;mt&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering i BiH sker p&#xe5; ett &#xf6;ppet, ansvarstagande, j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;llt och inkluderande s&#xe4;tt genom programmet (FIGAP2)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the gender mechanisms of Bosnia och Herzegovina (Gender Equality Agency on state level and two gender centers on entity level). The objective of the contribution is to have a standardised gender mainstreaming in BiH in order to  reach a situation where public decisions improve the conditions for women, men, girls and boys equally. The standardized gender mainstreaming should be done through a transparent, accountable, equitable and inclusive programme (FIGAP2).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The intervention aims at - &quot;public decisions to improve the conditions of women, men, girls and boys equally&quot;. This should be done by standardisation of gender mainstreaming in Bosnia and Herzegovina (through transparent, accountable, equitable and participatory FIGAP2). There are four objectives of the programme, which all aims at improving gender equality aspects of public decisions in BiH:
1. An accountable GE policy framework in FIGAP priority areas (GBV, Economic Empowerment, public participation)&#xa0;
2. Capable GM structures for GE that perform according to their mandate
3. Effective systems that support the accepted GM approach
4. Competent and sustainable staff contingency in BiH to promote and manage GM agenda</narrative>
  </description>
